## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical AWS knowledge of private content delivery, CloudFront with OAI, and Lambda@Edge integration, plus a tangible test plan.

## Key Concepts
- CloudFront Origin Access Identity (OAI)
- S3 bucket policies restricting GetObject to OAI only
- TLS enforcement and viewer protocol policy
- Lambda@Edge for header augmentation
- End-to-end testing of CDN delivery vs direct S3 access

## Code Example
```javascript
'use strict';
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const request = event.Records[0].cf.request;
  const tenantId = (request.headers['x-tenant-id'] && request.headers['x-tenant-id'][0].value) || 'unknown';
  request.headers['X-Tenant-Id'] = [{ key: 'X-Tenant-Id', value: tenantId }];
  return request;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate the CloudFront OAI and keys securely?
- How would you test the bucket policy with simulated access from non-CloudFront principals?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable, compliant multi-tenant real-time pipeline with data residency requirements, cross-account access, and disaster recovery.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation and per-tenant data locality
- Exactly-once delivery semantics across streaming and storage
- Cross-account IAM with STS and least privilege
- DR planning across regions, cost-aware choices
- Observability with CloudWatch, X-Ray

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: idempotent event handler skeleton
async function handleEvent(evt){
  const key = evt.tenant_id + ':' + evt.event_id;
  const exists = await db.get(key);
  if(exists) return; // idempotent
  await db.put(key, true);
  // process
}
```

